  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output A.1. Enhanced decent work statistics using innovative sources and statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">In 2019 the Household Income and Expenditure Survey (HIES) of the Marshall Islands (MHL) was conducted being only the second such survey, with the previous one being done in 2002. Significant information was collected on the country&#x2019;s labour market in line with the latest standards from the 19th International Conference of Labour Statisticians (19th ICLS), using an ILO-SPC standard labour force module developed for the Pacific island countries. The HIES 2019 was implemented during 12 months from April 2019 to March 2020.

In 2021 the country requested ILO technical assistance to prepare a labour market monograph from the survey, and the labour force monograph was finally completed and published in 2022. In addition to preparing the labour force module for HIES, the ILO provided technical assistance to Marshall Islands in preparing and producing relevant data from the 2019 HIES for input into the labour force report. ILO provided both financial and technical assistance in preparing the report on the labour force. In close collaboration with The Pacific Community &#x2013; Statistics for Development Division (SPC/SDD) and the Government of Marshall Islands Economic Policy, Planning and Statistics Office (EPPSO), and with guidance by the ILO, Marshall Islands Compendium of Analysis of the 2019/20 HIES was finalised and published in 2022, including a full section on its labour force.</narrative>
   </description>
